The least solution of the equation that adjoins the unit, two named elements, and the pointwise square is the submonoid generated by those two elements.

The generated submonoid contains the unit and both generators and is closed under multiplication, so the operator sends it into itself, and the least fixed-point set is contained in every such pre-fixed point. Conversely, the fixed-point equation makes the least fixed-point set a pre-fixed point, and it contains both generators, so the submonoid it determines contains the generated submonoid.
